igured it  out but it started back up again in a  later room at the level I found out he  was gonna do it every time he touched  the ground  so I had to complete ten minutes of this  level without ever standing on the floor  is that a Zeppelin  this isn't Gotham City what's that doing  here I'm a weapon  oh my god it's him Bruce Campbell's say  you can do fun side missions for Bruce  Campbell who plays a weirdo reporter  that wants to film you doing sick bball  moves it's like a dude perfect video  there's a nice return to a simpler time  here this one feels a lot more video  gaming if you know what I mean  you get unlockable costumes from taking  pictures of these Spyder logos  everywhere and you can collect comic  book covers like in the ps1 games except  this time you can actually read those  comics you'll end up picking them up as  often as the stupid spider tokens you  know spider-man never really struck me  as the type who would like comics or  even TV for that matter I feel like he  just has too much [ __ ] to do all day to  watch TV or read books why ulcer his  reference is always so dated I also like  using the unlockable costumes ah [ __ ]  not you again I switched into the suit  from the 2002 spider-man at the closet  in the game's hub area because I was  feeling nostalgic from my childhood  well I guess I can't change back now can  i [ __ ]  I'm stuck in this thing now which I'm  sure pisses off Sony a little but you  know hey it's their fault for putting it  in the game speaking of nostalgia one of  the boss fights is almost identical to  one from spider-man three though that  isn't exactly my definition of a fond  childhood memory and much like  spider-man 3 the bosses are all sort of  bland you either have dumb aerial  battles with robots that would give most  people motion sickness where you do  other fight son ceremoniously in a  parking lot how exciting  Rhino you fight him in a parking lot  lizard fight him in a parking lot  Captain America flight